      "category": "security",
      "source": "docs.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-07-30",
      "tags": ["sso", "saml"],
      "priority": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "security-005",
    "text": "This walkthrough shows how to connect Acme Cloud to Okta in under ten minutes. Create an Okta app, copy the metadata URL, and paste it into the SSO settings. Enable the sign-on policy and invite a small pilot group first. Watch out for clock skew, which is the most common SAML failure.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "SSO setup guide",
      "category": "security",
      "source": "blog.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-06-25",
      "tags": ["sso"],
      "priority": 3
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "security-006",
    "text": "Turn on multi-factor authentication to protect accounts with a second factor. Admins can enforce MFA per group in the Security policy page. Users can register a TOTP authenticator app or a hardware key. MFA is required for accounts with SSO enforced.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Multi-factor authentication",
      "category": "security",
      "source": "docs.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-03-22",
      "tags": ["mfa", "sso"],
      "priority": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "billing-001",
    "text": "Invoices are generated on the first day of each month and appear in Billing > Invoices. To download an invoice, select the billing period and click Download PDF. You can also enable email delivery of invoices to your billing address. Contact billing@acme.com if any line items look incorrect.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Downloading invoices",
      "category": "billing",
      "source": "docs.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-07-22",
      "tags": ["invoice", "billing"],
      "priority": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "billing-002",
    "text": "Credits are applied to your invoice in the order they expire. Usage is metered daily and shown as line items on the next invoice. You can see a live usage preview under Billing > Cost explorer. Invoices older than 24 months are only available on request.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Billing FAQ: credits and invoicing",
      "category": "billing",
      "source": "help.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-03-15",
      "tags": ["invoice", "credits"],
      "priority": 2
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "billing-003",
    "text": "Your monthly invoice lists compute, storage, and data transfer charges. Reserved instances appear as separate line items with a discount. We break down per-project costs so you can allocate spending to teams.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Understanding your Acme invoice",
      "category": "billing",
      "source": "blog.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-01-30",
      "tags": ["invoice"],
      "priority": 3
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "billing-004",
    "text": "I was missing line items too. The PDF only includes summary totals; expand the CSV export to see per-resource rows. Export from Billing > Invoices > Export CSV.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Re: Invoice PDF missing line items",
      "category": "billing",
      "source": "forum.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-05-11",
      "tags": ["invoice"],
      "priority": 4
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "api-001",
    "text": "The Acme API allows 10 requests per second per token by default. Bursts are allowed up to 30 requests within a five-second window. When you exceed the limit, the API returns 429 with a Retry-After header. Raise the limit by upgrading your plan or contacting support.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Rate limits and throttling",
      "category": "api",
      "source": "docs.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-09-01",
      "tags": ["rate-limits", "api"],
      "priority": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "api-002",
    "text": "Use OAuth 2.0 client credentials to obtain an access token for machine-to-machine calls. Send the token in the Authorization header as Bearer. Tokens expire after one hour; refresh with a new client-credentials request. Scopes limit each token to the resources your application needs.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Authenticating with OAuth2",
      "category": "api",
      "source": "docs.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-05-20",
      "tags": ["oauth2", "sso", "security"],
      "priority": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "api-003",
    "text": "Tokens expiring hourly is expected behaviour. Cache the token and refresh it in the background before expiry instead of requesting a new one on every call. Store the client secret in your secret manager, not in code.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Re: OAuth token expires every hour",
      "category": "api",
      "source": "forum.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-07-05",
      "tags": ["oauth2"],
      "priority": 4
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "api-004",
    "text": "Rotate API keys on a schedule and keep an inventory of where each key is used. Create the replacement key first, update your services, then revoke the old key after a grace period. Never embed keys in client-side code or public repositories.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "API key rotation best practices",
      "category": "api",
      "source": "blog.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-02-14",
      "tags": ["api-keys", "security"],
      "priority": 3
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "api-005",
    "text": "Webhooks deliver events such as invoice.paid and key.rotated to your endpoint. Sign each payload with the HMAC secret shown in the Webhooks settings. Respond with 2xx within five seconds; deliveries are retried with exponential backoff up to five times.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Webhooks reference",
      "category": "api",
      "source": "docs.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-09-10",
      "tags": ["webhooks", "api"],
      "priority": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "net-001",
    "text": "Acme Cloud resources run in a private VPC by default. Peer VPCs to share traffic between projects or with your on-premises network. Use a transit gateway when more than five VPCs must communicate. Peering is free, but cross-region traffic is billed per GB.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Private networking and VPC peering",
      "category": "networking",
      "source": "docs.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-04-18",
      "tags": ["vpc", "networking"],
      "priority": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "net-002",
    "text": "If a resource is unreachable, check the security group rules, then the route table, and finally the VPC peering status. Ping the private IP from a bastion host in the same VPC. Verify that outbound rules allow the destination port.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Troubleshooting connectivity",
      "category": "networking",
      "source": "help.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-08-02",
      "tags": ["connectivity"],
      "priority": 2
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "gen-001",
    "text": "Acme Cloud is a managed platform for compute, storage, and networking. Deploy containers, databases, and serverless functions in minutes. Every resource is metered per second and appears on the monthly invoice.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Acme Cloud platform overview",
      "category": "general",
      "source": "docs.acme.com",
      "date": "2024-01-10",
      "tags": ["overview"],
      "priority": 1
    }
  }
]

